This directory contains ciphertext only.

WireGuard host bundles live at wireguard/hosts/<immutable-node-id>.sops.yaml.
Each bundle contains that node's private key, only the PSK copies required by topology.requiredLinks, and the byte-exact base64-encoded canonical K3s server token when the node has a K3s role. Agent imports never trust a local agent token; populate them with `copy-k3s-token` from an existing server.
Every bundle must be encrypted to three recipients: the target host age identity, one shared online operator identity for routine SOPS operations, and one shared offline recovery identity. Plaintext workspaces and the remote staging tree exist only on tmpfs. `stage-secrets` asks the target host to create machine-bound systemd encrypted credentials under `/var/lib/homelab-secrets/generations/<generation>`, atomically switches `active`/`previous`, and verifies each credential before activation. Plaintext keys and tokens never enter the Nix store or persistent storage.
The online operator and offline recovery placeholders in topology are intentional hard gates. Replace both before importing any secret. The target host recipient is read directly from its host-local age identity.

Kubernetes bootstrap credentials live at kubernetes/<cluster>-bootstrap.sops.yaml.
Never commit plaintext, generated QR/PNG files, age identities, decrypted generations, or migration receipts.
